     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I recommend calling a human operator. I can't confirm the tube atmosphere because a sensor the growth stage needs isn't fitted, so I've marked the run UNKNOWN, not NORMAL.\n\n- **What I can't check:** tube pressure. The pressure gauge isn't installed, so pressure has read null the whole run. That means I can't confirm pressure is where it should be or rule out a blocked exhaust.\n- **What looks normal:**\n  - **Temperature:** it tracked the ramp and briefly overshot to 760.1 °C at the start of growth. It then settled and has held 749.7–750.2 °C against the 750 °C setpoint.\n  - **Oxygen:** it purged down from about 28,800 ppm to single digits and stays at 3–7 ppm during growth. That argues against air leaking in.\n  - **Argon flow and heater power:** argon is steady near 100 sccm and heater power is steady at about 45%.\n- **Scientific result:** not available yet, since the sample hasn't been characterized.\n\nAn independent pressure check, such as a temporary gauge or a look at the exhaust bubbler or backpressure, would let me resolve this."
     }
